<h4><i class="fa fa-bell" aria-hidden="true"></i> Browser Web Push <span class="label label-info"><i class="fa fa-flask" aria-hidden="true"></i> Labs</span></h4><p>After email verification, subscribers can enroll up to four browsers. Push uses standards-based payload encryption and VAPID; browsers must grant notification permission. Provider acceptance does not prove a notification was displayed.</p><button type="button" class="btn btn-default" data-browser-key>Generate VAPID key</button><p>Queue browser announcements from Devices and response providers or use the Control API’s <code>browser_recipient_ids</code>. Browser and operating-system behavior requires local acceptance testing.</p><p>There is no public signup, cross-participant roster browsing, SMS login, managed mustering, visitor tracking, geofencing or mobile push.</p>
